---
// CORE VISUAL - the claim gate.
//
// This is the proof philosophy in one figure: two questions, and a claim is only permitted when
// both answer yes. It replaces several paragraphs of "what this is not" disclaimer.
//
// The caption must stay a statement about CLAIM DISCIPLINE, not about the architecture's reach.
// "This is why ByteLite does not promise that every file shrinks" would misdescribe the target -
// a smaller self-contained representation for every eligible source file is exactly what
// ByteLite is being built to achieve. The gate governs what may be CLAIMED today.
---

<figure class="rg" aria-labelledby="rg-caption">
  <ol class="rg-flow">
    <li class="rg-question">
      <p class="rg-q">Can the original be reconstructed exactly?</p>
      <div class="rg-branches">
        <p class="rg-branch rg-branch-no">
          <span class="rg-answer">No</span>
          <span class="rg-outcome">Fail. Do not claim.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="rg-branch rg-branch-yes">
          <span class="rg-answer">Yes</span>
          <span class="rg-outcome">Continue</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="rg-question">
      <p class="rg-q">Is the complete artifact smaller?</p>
      <div class="rg-branches">
        <p class="rg-branch rg-branch-no">
          <span class="rg-answer">No</span>
          <span class="rg-outcome">Preserve the original. No reduction claim yet.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="rg-branch rg-branch-yes">
          <span class="rg-answer">Yes</span>
          <span class="rg-outcome">Continue</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="rg-final">
      <span class="rg-mark" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
      Counted lossless reduction
    </li>
  </ol>

  <figcaption id="rg-caption" class="rg-caption">
    Both gates must pass before anything may be claimed. Where they do not yet pass, the honest
    result is to preserve the original and say so. This governs what ByteLite claims today
    &mdash; it is not a limit on what the architecture is being built to achieve.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
.rg { margin: 0; background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .875rem; padding: 1.75rem; }
.rg-flow { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
.rg-question { background: #07090f; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .625rem; padding: 1.125rem; }
.rg-q { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: #e4e7f2; margin-bottom: .875rem; line-height: 1.5; }
.rg-branches { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .625rem; }
@media (max-width: 620px) { .rg-branches { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.rg-branch {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .2rem;
  border-radius: .5rem; padding: .75rem .875rem; margin: 0;
  border: 1px solid;
}
.rg-branch-no { background: rgba(248,113,113,.04); border-color: rgba(248,113,113,.22); }
.rg-branch-yes { background: rgba(52,211,153,.05); border-color: rgba(52,211,153,.26); }
.rg-answer { font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.rg-branch-no .rg-answer { color: #f87171; }
.rg-branch-yes .rg-answer { color: #34d399; }
.rg-outcome { font-size: .875rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.5; }

.rg-final {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .625rem;
  font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 700; color: #34d399;
  background: rgba(52,211,153,.08); border: 1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.32);
  border-radius: .625rem; padding: 1.125rem; text-align: center;
}
.rg-mark { flex-shrink: 0; }

.rg-caption {
  margin-top: 1.25rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid #1a2235;
  font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.7;
}
@media (max-width: 600px) { .rg { padding: 1.25rem; } }
</style>
